# HexText License

HexText is distributed under a **reasonably open license**.
You are free to use, share, and adapt the mod as long as you follow the terms below.
If you’re simply playing with it, this license doesn’t concern you—enjoy the mod!

---

## TL;DR

### ✅ You **CAN**
- Fork and modify the code.
- Submit Pull Requests to this repository.
- Copy portions of this code for use in other projects.
- Write your own code that depends on HexText (e.g., addon mods, integrations).

### ❌ You **CANNOT**
- Redistribute HexText in its entirety, whether source or compiled.
- Create or distribute code that contains **50% or more Functionally Equivalent Statements\*** from this repository.

### ⚖️ You **MUST**
- Maintain a **visible public repository** of your code if it uses, derives from, or copies any part of HexText.
  You retain full rights to your own code, but it must remain open and visible.

---

## General Clauses

### Personal Permission
Direct permission may be granted **only** by **KAMKEEL**.
Permission does not imply endorsement.

### Waiver
Any restrictive clause in this license may be waived by personal permission (see above).

### Extensive Clause
This license applies to **HexText**, the **HexText website**, legacy versions, and **all code, assets, or binaries** found in this repository unless otherwise stated.

### Informal Clause
This license is **non-enforceable in court**.
I have no intention of suing anyone for violations.
At worst, I’ll ask you to correct your mistake.
However, if you use public distribution platforms (like CurseForge), your project may be taken down for non-compliance.
Also—don’t be a jerk.

---

## If You Want to **Distribute** HexText

“Distribution” means making available binaries, assets, or source code from the original sources as part of your modpack or other package.

### Attribution
You must credit **KAMKEEL** as the creator of HexText.
If you modify the mod, you must clearly indicate that changes were made.
A link back is optional but appreciated.

### Redistribution
You may **not** redistribute the entire source code unless it has been **heavily modified** as a whole.
No more than **50%** of the original codebase may be redistributed without express permission from **KAMKEEL**.

### Non-Monetary
You may **not** charge for access to the mod, directly or indirectly.
This includes:
- Ad-gated links (e.g., adf.ly or similar).
- Download hosts with ads that slow or block access.
- Paywalls of any kind.

Charging for in-game items or cosmetic features on a server does **not** count as distribution, but must still comply with Mojang’s Terms of Service.

---

## If You Want to **Feature** HexText

“Featuring” means showcasing HexText without distributing it (e.g., YouTube, streams, reviews).

### Thief Clause
Do not claim authorship of HexText.
Crediting **KAMKEEL** makes you cooler—but isn’t required.

---

## If You Want to **Use HexText Code or Assets**

Usage of HexText’s code or assets falls under the **Extensive Clause**.

### External Clause
Some portions of the codebase may have alternative licenses; you must respect them.

### Attribution
You must credit **KAMKEEL** as the creator of HexText.
If you modify any part of the code or assets, clearly state that you have done so.
A link back is optional but appreciated.

### Copyleft
Your project must be **open source**, allowing redistribution and modification.
Include a clause similar to this one in your own license.

---

\* **Functionally Equivalent Statements:**
Code that performs the same tasks in the same way, even if rewritten or refactored, counts toward this equivalence threshold.

---

### Summary

Use it.
Build with it.
Share your work.
Just don’t redistribute HexText wholesale, sell it, or hide your code.

